{
  "Name": "Rigol DM3058E Digital Multimeter (native RIGOL command set, USB/RS-232)",
  "IdnPattern": "DM3058",
  "Terminator": "\n",
  "Notes": "Built from docs/devices/rigol-dm3058e/programming-manual.md (RIGOL Programming Guide - DM3058/DM3058E Digital Multimeter, Jan. 2015), scoped to USB and RS-232 - the DM3058E has no GPIB or LAN interface (those are DM3058-only; :LXI and GPIB commands are excluded entirely). *IDN? reports the model as 'DM3058' even on a DM3058E unit - expected per the vendor's own worked example, not a misconfiguration. This instrument supports three switchable command LANGUAGES (CMDSET RIGOL|AGILENT|FLUKE, native RIGOL is the power-on default) - this profile documents RIGOL syntax only; if commands stop being recognized, check CMDSET? first. Setting any :MEASure:<type> range switches the instrument to Manual mode automatically, silently overriding :MEASure AUTO. :MEASure:FREQuency/:PERiod's range parameter selects an input VOLTAGE range (reusing the AC-voltage table), not a frequency/period range. Most :MEASure:<type>? value queries are unavailable while :FUNCtion2 (vice/secondary display) is active. Sending :UTILity:INTErface:RS232:BAUD over the RS-232 link you're reconfiguring breaks that connection as soon as it's applied - reconnect at the new rate afterward. SYSTem:ERRor? is FIFO and pops one entry per call - poll until it returns 0,\"No error\". Status-register bit-level layout (which bit means what) is not documented here; only the register read/write commands are.",
